= Utility (decision theory) — Simple =

Utility is a number used to represent how a model ranks outcomes or choices. If one outcome has higher utility than another, the model treats it as preferred under the assumptions being used. Utility does not automatically mean money or happiness.

'''Important boundary:''' utility ≠ money.

